think The win: a checkpoint chain of 5 windows of 64 blocks (320 facts, past the 256 ceiling) — each epoch a bounded Cord Dag sealed to a Knot then pruned, the next epoch continuing onto the Knot via continue_verified — folds to the byte-identical whole-history supply (issued 320) while the LIVE Dag never exceeds one window (64). Ground truth is a plain fold of all 320 issues from empty; states_match confirms the chain equals it.
think Two Rooms honesty held: asserted only the exact facts (total_facts > dag_ceiling; the ceiling refuses DagFull; final supply == ground truth; max_live == window < ceiling) and reported the amortization as a measured loom line in the binary's own output (total_facts=320 dag_ceiling=256 max_live_blocks=64 windows=5 live_ratio_x10=50 would_overflow=yes) — a 5.0x fewer live blocks than an un-checkpointed run would need, which the ceiling makes not merely costly but impossible. A wall-time benchmark stays a named later round.
